 "issue": 256,
 "issue_title": "**Chromatic dict mislabels BFL as EFL** `optical_system.py:396-398`  (`f_F/f_d/f_C` are BFLs)",
 "issue_body": "**Chromatic dict mislabels BFL as EFL** `optical_system.py:396-398`  (`f_F/f_d/f_C` are BFLs).",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/pmaasz/openLens/issues/256",
 "pr": 274,
 "pr_title": "fix(system): report true per-wavelength EFLs in chromatic dict",
 "pr_body": "calculate_chromatic_aberration filled f_F/f_d/f_C with BFL copies, so any consumer reading f_d as EFL got the back focal length (off by the t*P/n principal-plane term). Derive both BFL (-A/C) and EFL (-1/C) from one per-wavelength system matrix and store each under its own keys. Longitudinal/corrected semantics unchanged. Add regression test pinning f_d to the matrix EFL and off the BFL.",
 "fix_commit": "402e8c1e4ed25155ebfeaf2aa36a5533a3f00767",
